Z||000000||Monkeyman||10-15-2000||07:32 AM||||I accidently installed some internet spy program the other day.  This keeps a record of all of the sites I've been to.  (I thought it was something else.)  I tried to uninstall it, but it's nasty little pop-up window (reminds me that it's trying to do it's job) keeps popping up.  I did a hard drive search and came up with "SSYSTEM.EXE".  I tried to delete that and was told that it was something that runs other programs and couldn't be deleted (probably a good thing that I can't get rid of that?).  <P>How do I find the original program on my computer and how do I get rid of it once I find it?||||reg||5
Z||000001||batboy||10-15-2000||08:34 AM||||It's probably a type of memory resident program. If so, you have to "turn off" the program before you can uninstall it. Try pushing Ctrl-Alt-Delete and go into the task manager. Find the program, highlight it, end task, and then uninstall or deleting the program. Maybe your Mommy put it on your computer to check out how many porn sites you visit in a week.<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 10-15-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||10-15-2000||03:51 PM||||My mother hasn't even visited my house in months, but nice try. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I installed the program myself the other day thinking it was something else.  I turned the program off like you said and so far it hasn't returned to bother me, but I wonder if it will once I turn the computer off and then back on.  Only problem now is that I can't find the program anywhere to delete it.  It must be somewhere since it was there to turn off.||||reg||1
Z||000003||My7Fieros||10-15-2000||05:18 PM||||Worst case scenerio....dump everything you want onto a zip file, then run a recovery disk on your comp...serious pain in the a$$, and only a last resort.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Seanh||10-15-2000||07:08 PM||||Yes, If you restart your computer it will come back. Unless it bothers your computer work Id just leave it and "Let it do its job". I am not sure how to remove it though. Sorry.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||10-15-2000||07:30 PM||||I have no intention of dumping everything and starting over although I wouldn't have to start over at the beginning.  I just upgraded to ME and (supposedly) I can go back to when I upgraded.  If I don't save anything to other media, I'll lose only what I've saved since the upgrade.  I don't want to do that, but I might.  I don't want to let it run.  It doesn't affect my computer, but it's annoying and it's taking up space.||||reg||1
Z||000006||batboy||10-15-2000||08:01 PM||||See if there is a legimate uninstall routine for that program by going into "my computer" (double click on that desktop icon). Next go into "control panel" and then open "add/remove programs". Scroll down and see if that program is listed. If so, you can unistall using this method. If not, you have to track the files down and manually delete them. I'm guessing the files are hidden or else your kids would find and disable this program too easily if you really were spying on them.||||reg||1
